"An earlier lesson in this unit described four ways yin and yang relate to each other, but left out a principle that keeps those four relationships from turning into a rigid either-or system: even at their most opposed, yin and yang are never completely pure. Within what looks like solid yang, there's a portion of yin; within what looks like solid yin, there's a portion of yang. Chinese medicine names this \"yang within yin, yin within yang,\" and treats it less as a poetic flourish than as a working rule for how the two categories actually behave.": "3957d4a9e180",
"An earlier lesson in this unit described four ways yin and yang relate to each other, but left out a principle that keeps those four relationships from turning into a rigid either-or system: even at their most opposed, yin and yang are never completely pure. Within what looks like solid yang, there's a portion of yin; within what looks like solid yin, there's a portion of yang. Chinese medicine names this \"yang within yin, yin within yang,\" and treats it less as a poetic flourish than as a working rule for how the two categories actually behave. The clearest illustration is the body's own layout, read through this lens long before anyone applied it to physiology in the modern sense: the upper body, associated with yang because it's exposed and active, still has a yin aspect in the chest, which houses the heart and lung and is shielded rather than fully open; the lower body, associated with yin because it's more interior and stored, still has a yang aspect in the back, which is exposed to sun and cold in a way the chest is not. Neither half is ever assigned to one category without qualification. This matters because it blocks a tempting shortcut: labeling an entire category as simply \"yang\" or simply \"yin\" and stopping there. A yang-associated state can still carry a trace of yin feeding it from underneath, and a yin-associated state can still carry a flicker of yang trying to break through — often exactly the detail a purely either-or reading would miss. Reading for the minority element hiding inside the majority one is what keeps this framework from oversimplifying a system that was never meant to split cleanly in half.": "7ef1bcd3f964",
